      "answer": "At the end of chapter two, after renaming the farm from Manor Farm to Animal Farm and painting the Seven Commandments on the barn wall, Snowball called the animals to the hayfield to start the harvest. However, the three cows, who had not been milked for twenty-four hours, began to low loudly due to their full udders. The pigs then milked the cows, obtaining five buckets of milk. When the animals asked about the milk, Napoleon dismissed their concerns, emphasizing the importance of the harvest instead. After the animals worked in the hayfield and returned in the evening, it was noticed that the milk had disappeared.",
