      "answer": "At the beginning of Chapter II, three nights after old Major's death, his body is buried at the foot of the orchard. Following this, during the next three months, there is much secret activity as the more intelligent animals, inspired by Major's speech, begin preparing for the Rebellion he predicted. The pigs, recognized as the cleverest animals, especially Snowball, Napoleon, and Squealer, take the lead in teaching and organizing the others into a new belief system called Animalism. They hold secret meetings in the barn after Mr. Jones falls asleep to expound the principles of Animalism, facing initial resistance and skepticism from some animals. Over time, the pigs struggle to counteract lies spread by Moses the raven about a mythical Sugarcandy Mountain. Meanwhile, the cart-horses Boxer and Clover become faithful disciples who help spread the teachings. The chapter also notes that Mr. Jones's management of the farm has declined, with neglect evident in various ways, setting the stage for the forthcoming Rebellion.",
